{"id":"word:hebrew:H7704","type":"word","title":"שָׂדֶה","subtitle":"H7704 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a field (as flat)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׂדֶה (H7704) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 334 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׂדֶה (sâdeh) means a field (as flat) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 46."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׂדֶה","transliteration":"sâdeh","pronunciation":"saw-deh'","strong":"H7704","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7704","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הַ/שָּׂדֶ֖ה","הַ/שָּׂדֶה֙","בַּ/שָּׂדֶ֔ה","הַ/שָּׂדֶ֔ה","הַ/שָּׂדֶ֑ה"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",131],["HRd/Ncmsa",66],["HNcmsa",34],["HNcmsc",24],["HR/Ncmsc",21],["HR/Ncmpc",6],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",6],["HR/Ncmsa",6],["HNcmpa",5],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"a field (as flat)","usage":"country, field, ground, land, soil, × wild.","full":"H7704. sadeh שָׂדַי noun masculine Psa 96:12 field, land (rare original form of שָׂדֶה (q. v. below), only in poetry); &#8212; absolute ׳שׂ Jer 4:17 , שָׂדָ֑י Hosea 10:4 +; — 1 cultivated field Hosea 12:12 , also 10:4 (si vera lectio, but see Now), yielding food Deut 32:13 ; Lam 4:9 ; שׂ ׳שֹׁמְרֵי Jer 4:17 keepers, watchmen of a field. 2 home of wild beasts: שׂ ׳בְּהֵמוֺת Psa 8:8 ; Joel 2:22 , שׂ ׳חַיְתוֺ Isa 56:9 ; Psa 104:11 , שׂ ׳זִזִ 50:11 ; 80:14 . 3 plain, opposite mountain, Jer 18:14 ; (but dubious, Co Du שִׂרְיֹן ). 4 land , opposed to sea , Psa 96:12 (compare שָׂדֶה 3 ; || תֵּבֵל Psa 98:7 ). שָׂדֶה 318 noun masculine Lev 27:24 id. (ordinary contracted form Ges § 84 a f ); — absolute ׳שׂ Gen 2:5 (twice in verse) +; construct שְׂדֵה 14:7 +; suffix שָׂדִי Jer 32:7-8 , שָֽׂדְךָ Deut 11:15 +, שָׂדֶ֑ךָ 24:19 ; Lev 25:3 , etc.; plural שָׂדוֺת 1Sam 22:7 +, construct שְׂדוֺת Neh 12:29 ; also שְׂדֵי 2Sam 1:21 ; Isa 32:12 ; Ruth 1:1 8 t. (some might be singular = שְׂדֵה compare Ba ZMG xlii (1888), 351 SS Buhl; note, e.g. שְׂדֵי 1:6 a, = שְׂדֵה v b 4:3 ; but see Kö ii. 1, 77 ); suffix שְׂדֹתֶיהָ Neh 11:30 , etc.; also שָׂדֶיךָ 1Kin 2:26 , שָׂדֵינוּ Micah 2:4 ; &#8212; 1 open field , country: a. pasture-land Gen 29:2 ; 30:16 ; Exod 9:3 (all J), Deut 11:15 ; 1Sam 11:5 10 t. J, JE. b. unfrequented Gen 24:63 , 65 , exposed to violence 4:8 (J), 2Sam 14:6 ; Deut 21:1 ; 22:25 , 27 , to wild beasts Exod 22:30 (E), Ezek 33:27 . c. specifically home of beasts: 2Sam 17:8 ; Jer 14:5 ; especially phrase הַשּׂ ׳חַיַּת Gen 2:19-20 , 3:1 , 14 (all J) of beasts in General, and, of wild beasts, Exod 23:11 , 29 (E), Hosea 2:14 ; 2:20 ; 4:3 ; 13:8 ; Deut 7:22 ; Lev 26:22 (H), Job 5:23 (|| הָאָרֶץ חַיַּת ), + 16 t.; הַשּׂ ׳בֶּהֱמַת 1Sam 17:44 compare Joel 1:20 ; הַשּׂ ׳אַיְלוֺת Song 2:7 ; 3:5 , compare בַּשּׂ אֲשֶׁר ׳הַצְּבָיִם 2Sam 2:18 ; hunting-ground Gen 25:29 ; 27:3 , 5 (all J E), compare שׂ ׳אִישׁ 25:27 (J E; || צַיִד יֹדֵעַ אִישׁ ). d. yielding plants and trees: Gen 25:27 (JE), 30:14 (J), Exod 10:5 (JE), 2Kin 4:39 ; Ezek 21:2 ; 39:10 ; especially phrase הַשּׂ ׳עֵשֶׂב Gen 2:5 ; 3:18 (both J), + 6 t. + ׳ע ׳בַּשּׂ Zech 10:1 ; הַשּׂ ׳שִׂיח Gen 2:5 , שׂ ׳גֶּפֶן 2Kin 4:39 , שׂ ׳מַּקֻּעֹת V:39, הַשּׂ ׳צִיץ Isa 40:15 ; Psa 103:15 , הַשּׂ ׳צֶמַח Ezek 16:7 ; הַשּׂ ׳עֵץ (4 t. עֲצֵי ) Exod 9:25 (JE), Deut 20:19 ; Lev 26:4 (H) Isa 55:12 8 t.; 2Sam 1:21 see תְּרוּמָה , √ רום . e. stony , הַשּׂ ׳אַבְנֵי Job 5:23 . f. open country , outside of walled city Judg 9:32 , 42 , 43 , 44 ; 19:16 ; 1Sam 19:3 ; 20:5 , 11 (twice in verse); 20:24 , 35 ; 2Kin 7:12 ; Micah 4:10 ; as battle-ground Josh 8:24 (J), 2Sam 10:8 = 1Chr 19:9 ; 2Sam 11:23 ; 18:6 , outside of military camp 1Sam 4:2 ; 14:15 ; opposed to city (in formula) 1Kin 14:11 ; 16:4 ; 21:24 ; Jer 14:18 ; Ezek 7:15 ; אֶרֶץ שְׂדֵה Lev 25:31 ; as site of small town, country +? 1Sam 27:5 (opposed to royal city), compare 1Chr 27:25 ; of high places, בַּשּׂ ׳גְּבָעוֺת Jer 13:27 ; quite General, 1Sam 30:11 ; Jer 40:7 , 13 ; including road Judg 20:31 ; 1Kin 11:29 ; Jer 6:25 ; distinguished from road Num 22:23 (JE), 2Sam 20:12 ; outside houses and courtyards Exod 8:9 (P), 1Sam 25:15 ; ׳בַּשּׂ nearly = outdoors Exod 1:14 (P), Judg 13:9 ; of surface of country or ground, ׳בַּשּׂ Exod 16:25 (J E; = הַמִּדְבָּר עַלמְּֿנֵי V:14), compare 1Sam 14:25 ; so הַשּׂ לְַמְּֿנֵי ׳(אֶל) 2Kin 9:37 ; Jer 9:22 ; Ezek 29:5 (|| הַמִּדְבָּ֫רָה ), 32:4 ; 39:5 ; same phrase opposed to house, comfort, etc., 2Sam 11:11 ; Ezek 16:5 , opposed to city Lev 14:7 , 53 , opposed to tent Num 19:16 (all P), opposed to tent of meeting Lev 17:5 (H). g. = expanse of country, opposed to mountain, in phrase שׂ ׳מְרוֺמֵי Judg 5:18 ; בַּשּׂ ׳הֲרָרִי Jer 17:3 (of Jerusalem) is dubious; compare הַשּׂ ׳לְעִי Micah 1:6 ( Jer 18:14 see שָׂדַי ). 2 definite portion of ground , field, land: a. cultivated ground Gen 37:7 (E), 47:24 (J; הַשָּׂדֶה זֶרַע ), Exod 22:4 (3 t. in verse); 22:5 (E), Lev 27:16-17 , (P), Micah 3:12 (in simile) Ruth 2:2 47t., + תְרוּמוֺת שְׂדֵי 2Sam 1:21 , זָֿ֑רַע׳שׂ Ezek 17:5 , טוֺב שָׂדֶה V:8 good soil . b. as private property , Micah 5:2 ; 5:4 ; Isa 5:8 (twice in verse); Gen 47:20 (J), 23:9 , 11 , 13 (P) + 50 t., + 2Chr 26:23 (as burial-place); also (הַ)שּׂ ׳חֶלְקַת , see חֶלְקָה ; and ׳שׂ צֹפִים , see צפה . c. city-land, adjacent to city (town) and subject to its control: Gen 41:48 (E), Lev 25:34 (P), Josh 21:12 (P) = 1Chr 6:41 ; Neh 11:25 , 30 ; 12:29 , 44 ; specifically of Zoan Psa 78:12 ; 78:43 . d. territory of nation, tribe: Gen 32:4 ; Num 21:20 (both J E), Judg 5:4 ; Ruth 1:1-2 , Gen 14:7 13 t. + יִשׂ נִחֲלַת ׳שְׂדֵה Judg 20:6 . e. territory of king , 2Sam 9:7 ; 13:30 . 3 land , opposed to sea, 1Chr 16:32 (opposed to הַיָּם ; = שָׂדַי Psa 96:12 ), perhaps also mainland Ezek 26:6 , 8 (Co Krae Toy and others; not Sm). שִׂדִּים see שׂדד . שְׂדֵרָה see סדר above,","rootNote":"or שָׂדַי ; from an unused root meaning to spread out;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 46","keyReferences":["1Chr 1